{:db/id 17592186096615 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186096415 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/id #uuid "f61ac550-d62c-558f-b6d5-0d4c9aba8089" :question/math-academy-id "e-3629" :question/problem "Given that $y=4\\log_3 x,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we apply our formula for the derivative when the base of the logarithm is a number other than $e.$ By doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}&=\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{x \\ln 3}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{4}{x \\ln 3}.\n\n}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186097018 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fc74cbb-55e3-58fe-93f7-23d2f90e74b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id 17592186094082} {:answer/id #uuid "c8eb47da-1745-5e7e-9737-588db0279dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id 17592186094083} {:answer/id #uuid "27f824f3-9710-5d1e-89d8-290ab212a196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id 17592186094084} {:answer/id #uuid "38a4b8f7-dd90-5e68-8316-42e512e1e894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{1}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id 17592186094085} {:answer/id #uuid "4599b2f9-9707-597b-9797-37f1b2b1555a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id 17592186094086}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5630eeac-2ac2-529f-8c22-77ea989d69be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186094081}] :question/id #uuid "f06ecd5e-5944-5764-a8e8-9da3fea992d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-11903" :question/problem "Given that $y = x - 3\\log_{5} x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$."} {:db/id 17592186097019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6f74602-324e-53ca-838c-8b274a97bc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x - \\frac{7}{x\\ln 9}" :db/id 17592186094088} {:answer/id #uuid "bb439b88-d8d5-5ce1-97d2-fff353d9a6cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id 17592186094089} {:answer/id #uuid "e85a174f-b0d2-5831-bff8-3555b6382def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x - \\frac{1}{x\\ln 9}" :db/id 17592186094090} {:answer/id #uuid "16661e50-45a6-585e-90ce-2d427494b71b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{1}{x\\ln 9}" :db/id 17592186094091} {:answer/id #uuid "21e9072b-91cf-598e-9f41-3597bcbc89ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{7}{x\\ln 9}" :db/id 17592186094092}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f26be675-4841-5853-9c73-242d275f5343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186094087}] :question/id #uuid "5483eb06-46ab-500c-9fb8-8d630575623c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11907" :question/problem "Given that $y = x^{2} - 7\\log_{9} x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$."} {:db/id 17592186233051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d746064f-9bc3-5f26-9c93-afaf01c3e7e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-101719" :question/problem "Given that $y=7-4{log}_{3}x$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}3}.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-4{log}_{3}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7)-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{3}x) \\\\  & =0-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{x\\operatorname{ln}3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1/\\operatorname{ln}3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1/\\operatorname{ln}3} & ={(-\\frac{4}{x\\operatorname{ln}3})\\,|}_{x=1/\\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186233900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7910af85-fe7d-5c72-bfa8-012147c4fad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id 17592186232810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7910af85-fe7d-5c72-bfa8-012147c4fad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id 17592186232810} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a0533ea-5c3b-54d0-8191-c267a1815911" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186232809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2dd8674-7fa4-5d68-955d-c19f5b7e1758" :question/math-academy-id "q-339989" :question/problem "Given the function $y=4{x}^{2}-6{log}_{3}x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{2}-6{log}_{3}x) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2x-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =8x-\\frac{6}{x\\operatorname{ln}3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(8x-\\frac{6}{x\\operatorname{ln}3})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =8(1)-\\frac{6}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =8-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186233901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dcaf086-29eb-58e3-9792-842c7a25fb05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id 17592186232812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dcaf086-29eb-58e3-9792-842c7a25fb05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id 17592186232812} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4aa8b73-2643-5d54-9ecf-8c68f6f1aaca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186232811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0ddc214-9263-5104-9473-b379b6f7ec26" :question/math-academy-id "q-339997" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={log}_{7}x-3\\operatorname{ln}x$, find ${f}^{'}(x).$\n\n${f}^{'}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{7}x-3\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{7}x)-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-3(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-\\frac{3}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186241022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0442097d-1b68-55b7-9cb8-c462931d1330" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id 17592186238117} {:answer/id #uuid "0e522cac-c75a-5c1f-9bac-01ed6857debd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{ln⁡5}" :db/id 17592186238178} {:answer/id #uuid "44b6755c-aead-5542-8a1b-64818f1fbff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id 17592186238650} {:answer/id #uuid "461da220-919b-5435-93cc-a2ea3dad39d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186238664} {:answer/id #uuid "ffca6930-a453-5efc-ba11-64e5e1be934c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id 17592186240327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0442097d-1b68-55b7-9cb8-c462931d1330" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id 17592186238117} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bea711e-203a-5f4c-8d6c-0248b489ff5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a3193e7-39e5-59fc-a3d8-c6e491fa4479" :question/math-academy-id "q-105256" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={7}^{x}+{log}_{5}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({7}^{x}+{log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & ={7}^{x}\\cdot ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5} \\\\  & ={7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186253529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010fae26-d218-5d85-80be-b5da7fa03138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}" :db/id 17592186250562} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7274d3-9d6c-566f-8ab0-5d6dadc206db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4x}" :db/id 17592186250801} {:answer/id #uuid "3fea77d7-dd38-54a3-ab38-de4a5e6af670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡5}" :db/id 17592186251082} {:answer/id #uuid "90d31982-431c-5c96-9fd1-28cbe6930c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}" :db/id 17592186251788} {:answer/id #uuid "e56177c0-fb1c-54a8-8c75-934ef63a1c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id 17592186252561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d31982-431c-5c96-9fd1-28cbe6930c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}" :db/id 17592186251788} :answer-field/id #uuid "35ef16c9-7f8c-57e6-86fd-b4dbee5a6bfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186252894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9de855f-8e10-5bff-89a6-c3649ce380b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11900" :question/problem "Given that $y=5{log}_{4}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186287936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d6c7d7-cbc8-50f3-a344-45446b405f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id 17592186284858} {:answer/id #uuid "2557b0d8-9f3c-5e2b-a795-8eef0be2c846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id 17592186285117} {:answer/id #uuid "265b440a-0541-5605-93d6-05c026a9c562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id 17592186285122} {:answer/id #uuid "7663eb58-65d7-5b9c-a07b-0641ecb1169d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186285889} {:answer/id #uuid "eb874120-2ccd-5cec-a284-10e8ad025134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id 17592186286946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08d6c7d7-cbc8-50f3-a344-45446b405f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id 17592186284858} :answer-field/id #uuid "2efe99a9-b212-56ab-a943-1bebc7a16391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186287245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "884748ff-1cf0-5818-a246-3daa4fae09f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-1921" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={2}^{x}+\\operatorname{log}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x}+\\operatorname{log}⁡x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10} \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186297309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a21d7c1-657b-5c7c-bc8d-a5a78f0a5e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}3}-4+5e" :db/id 17592186295600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a21d7c1-657b-5c7c-bc8d-a5a78f0a5e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}3}-4+5e" :db/id 17592186295600} :answer-field/id #uuid "24fc67ac-4879-57d5-8bd2-d439a30262bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186296699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8688ee43-a87d-5757-aeae-1697946d83af" :question/math-academy-id "q-308866" :question/problem "Given the function  $y=2{log}_{3}⁡x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+5{e}^{x},$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{log}_{3}⁡x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{4}{x}+5{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{4}{x}+5{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{4}{1}+5{e}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-4+5e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186314898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277904a9-9e9e-53f0-a87c-616303962482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}6}" :db/id 17592186312275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "277904a9-9e9e-53f0-a87c-616303962482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}6}" :db/id 17592186312275} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb11537-ff22-5776-85db-c4e4d92da407" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186314045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9fb0b98-97be-5fa4-a0a8-73b036fd9d03" :question/math-academy-id "q-339994" :question/problem "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+1-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡6} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =6(3)^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot ln⁡6} \\\\  & =55-\\frac{1}{ln⁡6}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186314913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a1b399-700a-5dd2-967b-49969d3534b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(10)}" :db/id 17592186312291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29a1b399-700a-5dd2-967b-49969d3534b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(10)}" :db/id 17592186312291} :answer-field/id #uuid "38b53a32-4b9b-556b-afd9-471f5f44697e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186314162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6065f3ff-ff9c-5643-832d-8d1ba7e4dfa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-340105" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}+log⁡x$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}+log⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(log⁡x) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}ln⁡(3)+\\frac{1}{xln⁡(10)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186314914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cea7a0d-5e57-5d82-b9dc-783b5889bf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}+\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}(5)}" :db/id 17592186312833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cea7a0d-5e57-5d82-b9dc-783b5889bf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}+\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}(5)}" :db/id 17592186312833} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b6adce3-ac95-53df-964b-74afaf250503" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186314381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05a9cae0-c21b-5778-9f36-154aaf19469f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340106" :question/problem "Given that $y=-{e}^{x}+3{log}_{5}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{x}+3{log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡(5)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}+\\frac{3}{xln⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}
